1
00:02:09,759 --> 00:02:10,560
Jingyan.

2
00:02:12,880 --> 00:02:14,400
Why is it you?

3
00:02:14,960 --> 00:02:16,620
What are you doing at my house?

4
00:02:17,160 --> 00:02:19,160
I brought you guys some fruit.

5
00:02:19,640 --> 00:02:20,079
Wait,

6
00:02:20,400 --> 00:02:21,930
what are you two doing here?

7
00:02:23,520 --> 00:02:24,680
Us...

8
00:02:26,600 --> 00:02:27,320
We...

9
00:02:27,920 --> 00:02:28,720
We...

10
00:02:30,320 --> 00:02:31,520
We were going to cook.

11
00:02:31,760 --> 00:02:32,320
Right.

12
00:02:32,800 --> 00:02:33,400
Cooking.

13
00:02:35,040 --> 00:02:35,840
And then,

14
00:02:36,360 --> 00:02:37,420
the power tripped.

15
00:02:37,440 --> 00:02:37,880
Right.

16
00:02:38,240 --> 00:02:38,900
It tripped.

17
00:02:39,200 --> 00:02:39,840
Tripped.

18
00:02:39,840 --> 00:02:40,480
Cooking?

19
00:02:41,480 --> 00:02:42,280
You two?

20
00:02:44,840 --> 00:02:46,400
That's a first.

21
00:02:50,800 --> 00:02:52,930
Shiya and I are getting divorced soon.

22
00:02:53,480 --> 00:02:55,079
She will move out in a couple of days.

23
00:02:55,079 --> 00:02:57,610
I asked her to teach me how to cook a few dishes,

24
00:02:57,640 --> 00:02:59,240
afraid I'll starve to death.

25
00:02:59,640 --> 00:03:00,480
Pei Song,

26
00:03:00,720 --> 00:03:02,580
if you had realized this earlier,

27
00:03:02,760 --> 00:03:04,690
you wouldn't be getting a divorce.

28
00:03:07,320 --> 00:03:08,320
Let me tell you,

29
00:03:08,760 --> 00:03:09,720
many people say

30
00:03:09,720 --> 00:03:11,200
if you want to capture someone's heart...

31
00:03:11,200 --> 00:03:12,730
You have to win her stomach.

32
00:03:12,960 --> 00:03:15,360
It doesn't mean you have to know how to cook everything,

33
00:03:15,360 --> 00:03:17,079
but rather when you are cooking,

34
00:03:17,079 --> 00:03:19,520
you can have some physical contact.

35
00:03:20,480 --> 00:03:21,210
For example,

36
00:03:21,400 --> 00:03:22,860
when cutting vegetables,

37
00:03:23,200 --> 00:03:24,329
you cut your finger.

38
00:03:24,640 --> 00:03:25,600
When frying,

39
00:03:26,320 --> 00:03:27,450
oil splashes on you.

40
00:03:28,320 --> 00:03:30,800
Or you can tie each other's aprons.

41
00:03:31,440 --> 00:03:33,640
It's not about making you a chef.

42
00:03:34,840 --> 00:03:35,600
And,

43
00:03:36,120 --> 00:03:38,720
we women value men and women working together,

44
00:03:39,000 --> 00:03:40,040
making the work less tiring.

45
00:03:40,040 --> 00:03:42,170
What we want is this sense of security.

46
00:03:43,000 --> 00:03:44,060
Sense of security.

47
00:03:44,560 --> 00:03:45,820
Who told you to be here?

48
00:03:45,880 --> 00:03:46,480
Of course,

49
00:03:46,920 --> 00:03:48,040
if you can cook,

50
00:03:48,440 --> 00:03:49,570
that's even better.

51
00:03:50,200 --> 00:03:50,760
Right?

52
00:03:55,160 --> 00:03:56,480
Shiya.

53
00:03:59,040 --> 00:04:00,970
Is your mom feeling better lately?

54
00:04:01,040 --> 00:04:02,240
Keep your voice down.

55
00:04:02,560 --> 00:04:03,600
Why hasn't she told you yet?

56
00:04:03,600 --> 00:04:05,860
What did you say happened to Shiya's mom?

57
00:04:06,880 --> 00:04:08,680
Let Shiya tell you herself.

58
00:04:09,040 --> 00:04:09,970
I'm leaving now.

59
00:04:11,560 --> 00:04:12,200
Go ahead.

60
00:04:14,240 --> 00:04:15,240
Behave yourself.

61
00:04:20,200 --> 00:04:21,660
What happened to your mom?

62
00:04:57,880 --> 00:04:58,320
Shiya.

63
00:04:58,680 --> 00:04:59,080
Shiya.

64
00:04:59,320 --> 00:05:00,720
Please save your brother.

65
00:05:00,720 --> 00:05:02,240
Your brother is dying.

66
00:05:02,840 --> 00:05:04,640
Your brother owes a lot of money.

67
00:05:04,680 --> 00:05:06,340
They kidnapped your brother.

68
00:05:06,400 --> 00:05:07,680
They said if he can't pay back the money,

69
00:05:07,680 --> 00:05:09,340
they'll make him a scapegoat.

70
00:05:10,120 --> 00:05:11,920
Aren't you the daughter-in-law of the Pei family?

71
00:05:11,920 --> 00:05:13,160
Only you can save him.

72
00:05:17,360 --> 00:05:18,760
I already saved him once.

73
00:05:19,040 --> 00:05:20,760
I've paid for his mistakes too.

74
00:05:20,760 --> 00:05:22,200
He brought this all on himself.

75
00:05:22,200 --> 00:05:23,160
I'm incompetent.

76
00:05:23,160 --> 00:05:24,160
I can't save him.

77
00:05:24,440 --> 00:05:25,600
You should call the police.

78
00:05:25,600 --> 00:05:26,800
How can you be so cold-blooded?

79
00:05:26,800 --> 00:05:27,440
Song Shiya.

80
00:05:27,440 --> 00:05:28,440
We shouldn't have

81
00:05:29,000 --> 00:05:30,120
given birth to you.

82
00:05:32,200 --> 00:05:33,159
Cold-blooded?

83
00:05:34,120 --> 00:05:35,320
When you stole my identity

84
00:05:35,320 --> 00:05:36,720
to borrow from loan sharks for him,

85
00:05:36,720 --> 00:05:39,780
why didn't you say you shouldn't have given birth to me?

86
00:05:40,480 --> 00:05:41,120
Shiya.

87
00:05:41,560 --> 00:05:41,960
Mom.

88
00:05:42,080 --> 00:05:42,480
Mom,

89
00:05:42,680 --> 00:05:43,480
Shiya,

90
00:05:43,480 --> 00:05:44,409
I'm begging you.

91
00:05:44,600 --> 00:05:46,600
Save him one last time, please?

92
00:05:46,720 --> 00:05:47,120
Mom.

93
00:05:47,560 --> 00:05:50,680
Do you want your mother to kill herself right in front of you?

94
00:05:50,680 --> 00:05:51,080
Mom.

95
00:05:51,080 --> 00:05:52,440
Please save your brother.

96
00:05:52,440 --> 00:05:53,640
If you don't save him,

97
00:05:53,880 --> 00:05:54,880
we will expose your contract marriage

98
00:05:54,880 --> 00:05:56,600
with the Pei family.

99
00:05:56,920 --> 00:05:59,250
Let's see how the Pei family handles that.

100
00:06:04,080 --> 00:06:06,240
How can you be so shameless?

101
00:06:07,240 --> 00:06:08,680
Shiya.

102
00:06:09,920 --> 00:06:11,080
Don't be angry.

103
00:06:11,240 --> 00:06:13,320
Your father was just too anxious,

104
00:06:13,400 --> 00:06:14,730
that's why he said that.

105
00:06:15,440 --> 00:06:17,640
We have no other choice.

106
00:06:18,520 --> 00:06:19,650
You are a good child.

107
00:06:20,000 --> 00:06:23,200
You won't just stand by and watch your brother die, right?

108
00:06:23,960 --> 00:06:26,840
Just save him this one last time, okay?

109
00:06:28,520 --> 00:06:30,680
He was just trying to make money to pay off his debts.

110
00:06:30,680 --> 00:06:32,159
He was momentarily blinded

111
00:06:32,159 --> 00:06:35,290
and participated in that big data analysis experiment.

112
00:06:35,680 --> 00:06:36,880
We didn't expect them

113
00:06:37,360 --> 00:06:38,720
to all be scammers.

114
00:06:39,080 --> 00:06:40,400
Your brother's debt

115
00:06:40,600 --> 00:06:42,600
just kept growing.

116
00:06:53,120 --> 00:06:55,120
Here is some money I saved up before.

117
00:06:55,200 --> 00:06:57,000
Take it back and pay it off first.

118
00:06:57,840 --> 00:07:00,120
I will arrange temporary housing for you later.

119
00:07:00,120 --> 00:07:02,520
For now, just don't go out running around.

120
00:07:03,080 --> 00:07:04,400
Wait for me to contact you.

121
00:07:04,400 --> 00:07:05,130
Understand?

122
00:07:18,400 --> 00:07:19,080
Hello, Mom.

123
00:07:19,440 --> 00:07:20,040
Shiya,

124
00:07:20,480 --> 00:07:21,200
Song Shiya.

125
00:07:21,640 --> 00:07:23,500
Your brother committed suicide.

126
00:07:42,280 --> 00:07:43,940
After my brother passed away,

127
00:07:44,240 --> 00:07:47,040
Dad tried to get an explanation from those people,

128
00:07:47,280 --> 00:07:48,280
running around,

129
00:07:49,720 --> 00:07:51,250
but got into a car accident.

130
00:07:52,560 --> 00:07:54,200
Mom couldn't take the shock

131
00:07:54,960 --> 00:07:56,000
and lost her mind.

132
00:08:23,000 --> 00:08:24,000
I'm sorry.

133
00:08:25,800 --> 00:08:27,530
I didn't know about any of this.

134
00:08:33,120 --> 00:08:34,159
From now on,

135
00:08:35,080 --> 00:08:36,640
you won't be alone anymore.

136
00:08:44,800 --> 00:08:45,600
But

137
00:08:46,360 --> 00:08:48,420
I suspect things aren't that simple.

138
00:08:49,400 --> 00:08:51,760
So I've been investigating for the past six months,

139
00:08:51,760 --> 00:08:54,120
and I found out that Pei Ning is involved.

140
00:08:57,400 --> 00:08:59,530
I know he's always had feelings for me,

141
00:08:59,600 --> 00:09:01,240
so I used that to get close to him

142
00:09:01,240 --> 00:09:02,770
to find out what he was up to.

143
00:09:03,720 --> 00:09:05,480
I discovered he's been developing

144
00:09:05,480 --> 00:09:06,880
an AI algorithm.

145
00:09:09,800 --> 00:09:11,000
But if this algorithm

146
00:09:11,240 --> 00:09:12,920
falls into the wrong hands,

147
00:09:13,800 --> 00:09:16,400
there's a huge risk of personal privacy leaks.

148
00:09:24,960 --> 00:09:25,800
So,

149
00:09:27,640 --> 00:09:29,840
is that why you wanted a divorce?

150
00:09:34,120 --> 00:09:34,760
That was the only way

151
00:09:34,760 --> 00:09:36,620
he would drop his guard around me,

152
00:09:37,200 --> 00:09:39,000
so I could gather more evidence.

153
00:09:42,440 --> 00:09:43,680
But if you do this,

154
00:09:45,040 --> 00:09:46,360
you could be in danger.

155
00:09:47,400 --> 00:09:48,460
Aren't you afraid?

156
00:10:08,320 --> 00:10:09,120
If

157
00:10:09,520 --> 00:10:10,920
fate can't be changed

158
00:10:11,480 --> 00:10:12,810
and I'm destined to die,

159
00:10:13,280 --> 00:10:14,480
then I'll accept it.

160
00:10:15,720 --> 00:10:16,720
But until then,

161
00:10:17,560 --> 00:10:19,120
I absolutely won't just sit around and wait for it.
